WEBVTT

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.350
Our story jumps back to before Souma
Kazuya was summoned to this world.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.640
Up to then, the capital of Parnam had
expanded out in an unplanned fashion,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.650
with its streets zigzagging in winding
and convoluted directions.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:34.740
Souma laid out main roads and rebuilt
the city to make rapid logistics possible.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.070
Moreover, he built water
and sewage systems,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.240
and put efforts into beautifying the city.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.750
He further improved on public sanitation

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.830
by constructing large sedimentation
basins to purify the sewage.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.500
During the excavation work,
the bones of gargoyles, giants,

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.300
and countless other monsters
were discovered.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.640
Among them were the bones of a dragon.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.680
Just as they were about to be
taken to the Royal Academy,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.100
they suddenly turned up missing.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.110
Genia, you were the one behind that?

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.230
I am terribly sorry about this.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.360
But this was a long time ago.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.570
It would have been forgotten
if no one had mentioned it.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.360
Why bring it up now?

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.490
The fault rests with me in that regard.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.830
I was sorting through some of my papers,
and this was mixed in with them.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.000
"Dear Lu, I'm taking the dragon bones,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.340
so take care of the details
for me. Genia." Ah...

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.920
You just found that?
Took you long enough, Lu.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.590
After you stole the dragon bones
with a single scrap of paper,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.180
I don't want to hear it.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.470
It's mean of you to say I stole them.
That's why I left the note.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.140
Could you save the couple's
squabble until afterward?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.810
W-W-We are not a couple!

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.520
You don't want me as your wife?

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.150
N-No, I mean, we are not<i> yet </i>a couple!

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.530
So, what were you going to do
with the dragon bones?

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.830
I'm so glad you asked!

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.540
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:15.590
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:24.430
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:29.440
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.400
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.280
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:45.620
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.960
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.550
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:02.050
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.890
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:12.020
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.820
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:22.910
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:29.700
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.540
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.510
"Aping the Frown of Beauty"

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.510
This one's name is "Mechadra."

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.720
"Aping the Frown of Beauty"

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.720
It's a mechanical dragon I made
from monster components

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.300
and mystery parts that
I discovered in dungeons,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.850
patched onto a dragon skeleton.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.810
Going off of "monster components"
and "dungeon mystery parts,"

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.150
I can't help but have
a bad feeling about this.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.480
This isn't going to
start rampaging, is it?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.440
There's no way it could rampage.
It doesn't even move in the first place.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.070
Huh? It doesn't?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:09.160
Of course not. There's no critical
system to relay orders to each part.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.870
In that case, why did you make it?

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:17.840
I made it as an experiment to study
how the joints of living things work.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.510
See? The motion itself is this smooth.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.260
It doesn't take any strength
at all to move it.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.260
Yeah, that's amazing. It's amazing, but...

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.890
G-Genia, what kind of
monstrosity did you make?

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:32.770
If the Star Dragon Mountain Range
finds out about this,

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.520
it could become an international incident.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.520
It could?

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.860
When we get back, let's send a letter of
apology to the Star Dragon Mountain Range.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:45.360
Right. We might have to rebury the bones,
or have them sent back there.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.240
Mm-hmm.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.880
Whoa, King! Did you do something?!

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.210
Souma, you used your
Living Poltergeist, huh?

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.010
Yeah, I was just a little curious.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:11.010
I knew it! My calculations were correct!

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.680
Lu, take a look at how
the movements just flow!

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.230
That's not what the issue is here!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:20.980
And as for you, Your Majesty, moving
around a mechanical dragon like that

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.530
can only be taken as
a threat to other nations!

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.410
Still, can it even be weaponized?

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.700
Does the Mechadra have any armaments?

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:37.120
Not even I am crazy enough
to deliberately arm a model.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.090
Which means that there
really isn't any way to use it.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:43.050
It sucks to have something that
other countries would be wary of,

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:46.300
but have it be completely useless,
doesn't it?

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:53.640
For now, we will treat the Mechadra
as a top-secret internal matter,

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.310
and keep it locked down tight
until we hear

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.850
from the Star Dragon Mountain Range.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:57.890
Huh?

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.860
Consider yourself lucky you
aren't being thrown into a cell!

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.360
Genia Maxwell, we're going to build
a state research lab for you.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.400
I'll leave the theme of your
research there up to you.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.570
Do you mean it?

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:12.160
However, you'll have to provide
ten percent of the research funding.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:17.290
Ten percent? As the one who has been
paying for all her research up to now,

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:20.710
I would be grateful if you
would pay the whole amount.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.590
What if I did pay the whole amount?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:25.460
There's no telling what
she'd start researching.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.050
The Poncho Bridge got demolished.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.350
Huh? But that was convenient
when I had to go shopping.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.890
Things have been a lot stricter
since Prince Julius returned.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.770
The Gemstone Broadcasts
have been prohibited, too.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:48.070
And food is now being rationed. I don't
have enough to feed my children.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:51.870
Word going around is that those rations
are going to get reduced even more.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.320
Huh?

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:58.080
Aw, I wish His Majesty Souma
would occupy us again.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.300
There are a lot of complaints
among the people?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.300
That's just because I've returned lax
public morals to the way they were.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.430
They say a breach in the levee
starts with one ant hole, right?

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.220
The people will get too puffed up
if we don't clamp down on them.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.350
If they want to blame someone,

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.890
they can blame Elfrieden for
demanding so much in reparations.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.810
Don't blame the state;
that's barking up the wrong tree.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.770
What is it?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.820
Huddles, Lord of Galua, isn't it?

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:35.620
Your Highness, please help!
There's been an uprising!

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.700
What?

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.830
As you know, Galua is on
the outskirts of the country.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:44.460
We have little food, and some of my
people have even starved to death.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.840
Their discontent has exploded.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.720
Hmph, as I recall, Lord Huddles,

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.510
you refused to put your
trust in the young prince,

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.260
and instead reinforced your
own soldiers, did you not?

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.890
You can go ahead and defend yourself.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.770
But Your Highness!
The longer the riots continue,

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.730
the more discord will spread to
other quarters of the principality!

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:09.030
Besides, if you make
a show of strength now...

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.150
Hmm...

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.490
I am now taking lead of all of our forces
and putting down the rebellion in Galua!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.410
King, play with us!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.210
King!

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:28.000
Your Majesty, I'm happy that you are
here entertaining Rou and the others,

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.920
but aren't you too busy for this?

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:33.760
It's all right. I don't have a whole
lot of work at the moment.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.550
Is that right?

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.930
Then you can play with him
all you like, Rou!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.890
Right!

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.600
Now cut that out!

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.310
This is quite the sight, Master.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.400
Oh, you're the last one to
be calling me out, Carla.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.570
You look so out of place
in a maid outfit it's scary.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.620
Please don't say that!
That's what I think, myself.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.830
Isn't that skirt awfully short on you?

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.750
Please don't stare!

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.630
Th-The head chambermaid
told me to wear this.

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:13.880
Ah, so this is what Serina likes.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.010
Have you finished your
chambermaid training yet?

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.760
Tr-Training?

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.640
Wh-What happened?

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.180
She... She whipped me, with a real whip.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.560
A whip?

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.940
What's more, since it was a special whip,
enchanted with magic,

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:33.230
it didn't leave a mark on me,
even where it hit me.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.530
The whip is love. Love must be accepted.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.460
If Carla, whom even Gaius
himself trained, is afraid of her,

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.290
how bad must she be?

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.250
Carla...

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.250
Yes?!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:53.250
I thought I asked you to make up
His Majesty's bed in his office.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:58.260
C-Collecting the sheets of a man
I know is asking too much.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.060
What are you talking about?
If you are a chambermaid,

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.810
then in due time, when His Majesty and
the princess engage in [...],

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.730
and [...] their [...],

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.770
--L-Let's all go play over there, okay?
--you're going to have to make up
their soaking-wet bed

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:09.810
--Okay.
--Okay.
--you're going to have to make up
their soaking-wet bed

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.610
like it was no concern of yours at all.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:20.620
I see. So, did they put down the uprising?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.240
Yes. They suppressed them
in a fairly brutal manner,

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:26.580
probably to make an example of them.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.170
That's the wrong way to use brutality.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:33.130
That is only going to make
public discontent increase.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.170
Hakuya, what does
the emissary from Van say?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.430
The people's representative
from Van gave me this.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:49.690
"We, the people of Van, express allegiance
to the Kingdom of Elfrieden,

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.900
and request reinforcements"?!

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.660
Souma, was this something you figured on?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.240
I'll admit, I expected some movement.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:08.870
But I can't determine what conclusion
the people of Van will come to.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.580
However, now that we have
received a formal request,

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:15.130
the kingdom will accept it
and send reinforcements.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:28.310
Damn it! I never thought Van, of all
places--the city where I was born--

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:34.020
would betray me and start wagging
its tail for that despicable Souma!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:38.070
I bring word that the grand
nobleman Lord Cutlass

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:42.320
appears to have risen up to overthrow
the Amidonian royal family.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.910
He's what?!

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:48.660
Lord Schadler, who took in
the people who fled from Galua,

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.830
now defies our request for their return,

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.000
and is rising up in revolt
against Your Highness!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.250
The faction of nobles loyal
to Roroa are banding together

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.670
and demanding Your Highness's abdication!

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.210
Lord Schadler?!

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.590
He's rebelling?

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.760
The people are rising up
and moving on Galua!

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:06.810
What... is happening?

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:14.100
I see, so Julius's forces have fallen.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:17.070
It would be simply impossible
to put down rebellions like these,

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:20.190
when they come about all at once.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:24.990
Julius has allegedly taken a small force
with him and fled to the empire.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:28.870
So far, everything is going
as we expected...

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.790
...but haven't they gone
a little <i>too </i>well?

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.120
Watching the way that all of
these uncoordinated rebellions

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:37.630
have come about in unison the way they
have is something we never counted on.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:40.920
The "some other will at work"
that you mentioned?

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:55.400
After the expulsion of Julius, Amidonia
became a state without a leader.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:56.900
Seeking to take advantage of this

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:00.230
were the Lunarian Orthodox
Papal State to the north,

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:03.570
and the Republic of Turgis to the south.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:04.490
"Mercenary State Zem"

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.360
"Mercenary State Zem"

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.360
The Mercenary State Zem to the west

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.910
"Mercenary State Zem"

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.910
showed no sign of invading, in order
to maintain their perpetual neutrality,

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:14.040
but did send mercenaries
to the other two countries.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:14.790
"Lunarian Orthodox Papal State"

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.540
"Lunarian Orthodox Papal State"

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.540
The Lunarian Orthodox Papal State

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.840
is home to the Lunarian Orthodox Church,

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.340
which worships the moon goddess Lunaria,

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:26.800
and is a religious movement whose pope
presides over both church and state.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.140
In response to the rebellion
in the Principality of Amidonia,

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.930
they dispatched forces along
their border with Amidonia

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:35.640
to defend the adherents
within their nation.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:36.810
"Republic of Turgis"

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:40.610
"Republic of Turgis"

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:40.610
On the other hand, the Republic of Turgis
was a bitterly cold land.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.570
"Republic of Turgis"

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.570
The southern peninsula, in particular,

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:46.030
"Republic of Turgis"

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:46.030
was bound by ice and snow
for most of the year,

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:50.200
"Republic of Turgis"

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:50.200
and any land where it does not
snow is the envy of the nation.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:55.540
The principality is currently in disarray,
and ripe for invasion.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.630
Luckily, the advance of the
Republic of Turgis's forces

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.630
was halted by the brave fighting
of the aged General Herman

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.340
who boasted a century of experience
in war, and was the lord of Nelva,

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.300
a fortified city in the south.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:09.510
However, there was no telling
how long that would last.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:12.060
The Principality of Amidonia
without its crown prince

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:15.430
was now in an extremely
precarious position.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:19.940
They want the Kingdom of Elfrieden
to annex all of Amidonia?

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.900
Yes, sire. A joint request from
General Herman Neumann

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:26.780
and the former finance minister,
Gatsby Colbert,

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.070
has been officially delivered.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.320
I guess it's only natural

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.040
that they'd rather give themselves
over to the kingdom

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.660
than be divided up and conquered.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.750
If General Herman, the one
who stopped Turgis in its tracks,

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:42.960
and Colbert, the former finance
minister, support annexation,

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:45.420
then I doubt that anyone
would oppose them.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:48.760
Hakuya, is this your "other will at work"?

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.510
I cannot be certain, sire.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.010
So, what do we do?

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:55.140
What do we do, you're asking me?

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:58.770
There's a whole lot of downside
to annexing Amidonia.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:02.730
Let's start by looking for the upside.
Our population would increase,

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:06.230
and in the long run,
so would our national strength.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:09.530
Furthermore, Amidonia is rich
in material resources,

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:12.280
so we could look forward
to a stable supply of those.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:19.830
Now for the downside.
First, there's the food crisis.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.040
Things were going well
in Van, weren't they?

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:24.840
Van may be the capital,
but it's only one city.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.630
When it comes to Amidonia as a whole,

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:32.890
it's a lot to ask of our kingdom, when we
just barely solved our own food crisis.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:37.520
On top of that, it was a hostile
nation until just days ago,

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.600
so governing it will be difficult.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.940
Up to now, the Union of Eastern Nations,

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.610
the Principality of Amidonia,
and the Republic of Turgis

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:47.280
are the only nations that
we've shared a border with,

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.110
but now we'd have the Mercenary State Zem

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:52.320
and the Lunarian Orthodox
Papal State at our borders.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:57.290
The more countries we are adjacent to,
the more difficult diplomacy becomes.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:02.790
Mm-hmm. Also, while I wasn't
counting on them in the first place,

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:07.550
if we annex Amidonia, we won't be
receiving our war reparations any longer.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:11.760
Then we aren't annexing them?

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.760
I'd prefer it if possible,

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:19.270
but it seems that we have
no choice but to agree.

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:21.980
If we refuse, it will
upset our justification

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:27.650
that we integrated Van into the kingdom
at the request of its people.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:33.610
Mm-hmm. While we can admit Van,
we can't very well ignore the rest.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:37.330
Also, if the people of Van end up
forsaking their countrymen,

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.620
they will be disenchanted
with the kingdom.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.580
If we leave them to the invading
forces of the Republic of Turgis

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.170
and the Lunarian Orthodox Papal State,

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:48.960
our own country will be
overrun with refugees.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.210
In that case, it's better to
take them all in to begin with,

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:55.510
and start looking after them.
It may be a lot of work now,

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:59.510
but in the long run,
it's sure to be worth it.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:01.810
Seriously though, good grief.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:06.400
It is hereby decided that all of Amidonia
is to be admitted into the kingdom,

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.650
and all other nations are
to be made aware of this.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.940
Yes, sire.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:12.240
The naval forces under Excel's command

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.660
are to be sent alongside the border
with the Republic of Turgis,

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:18.410
where they will stand ready
to attack at any time.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:23.910
And so, the territories of
Amidonia were formally,

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:28.040
as well as peacefully, annexed
into the Kingdom of Elfrieden.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:32.630
Gatsby Colbert!

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:34.010
Sire!

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:38.550
Colbert, I commend you for bringing
the people of Amidonia together.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.810
Without your efforts, this turmoil
would have been prolonged,

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:46.020
and the people of Amidonia would
have suffered much misery.

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.900
Your words are too kind, sire.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.320
Be that as it may, Your Majesty,
I have something to deliver to you.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:57.360
These are the Principality of Amidonia's

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:01.450
internal income and expenditure reports,
as well as documentation of rights.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:05.830
They were kept in a safe place out
of fear of losing them during the war.

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:09.960
Whoa, hey, Julius was left in charge of
running the principality without those?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.500
I kind of feel sorry for him now.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:16.880
That is a wonderful gift.
Governing will be much easier now.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:21.100
However, you should take
those back with you.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.600
Huh?

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:28.140
Colbert, former finance minister of
Amidonia, are you willing to serve me?

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.270
Y-Yes, sire.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:35.610
You are hereby made finance minister
of the Kingdom of Elfrieden,

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:37.780
and charged with maintaining
the nation's finances.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:42.330
Just a moment, please! Don't you mean
overseeing Amidonia's finances?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.080
You are the finance minister
for the Kingdom of Elfrieden.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:49.290
B-But sire, I am an Amidonian.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:53.210
It doesn't matter. Using whomever
is useful, no matter who they are,

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:55.510
is now the Elfrieden way.

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.760
Y-Your Majesty...

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:00.050
Amidonia was not very well-off as it was,

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:04.310
and then had much of its budget taken
for military expenses. Nonetheless,

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:08.140
your skill in keeping the government
from going bankrupt has been marvelous.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.190
You are the kind of person I want,
by all means.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:15.230
Kingdom of Elfrieden
Finance Minister Colbert,

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:19.450
those documents will be
the tools of your trade.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:23.910
Take them with you, and work
to rebuild the lands of Amidonia.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:28.500
Y-Yes, sire. I understand.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.710
Herman Neumann!

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:36.130
I commend you for stopping
the army of the Republic of Turgis.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:40.340
Without your efforts, our relief efforts
would not have been in time,

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.890
and things would have been
consumed in terrible chaos.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:45.850
Warriors are those who defend the people.

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:48.890
That remains unchanged,
whether there is a ruler or not.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:52.350
I only did what I had to do.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:59.490
I, too, have something I'd like
to offer Your Majesty.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:04.320
However, once you receive it,
I hope that you will not return it.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.910
The southern region of Amidonia
has a thriving wool industry,

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.210
and produces fine quality wool.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:18.960
These are bolts woven from that wool.
I do hope that you will accept them.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:22.760
Ho... Do you mind if I
look at them up close?

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:24.220
As you please.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:33.810
It kind of feels like a carpeting, maybe.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:35.810
Hmm? Carpeting?

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.780
A rug, given as a gift...

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:44.780
Now why is it that it seems like
I've heard of this set-up before?

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:46.990
Tell me, Herman...

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:48.410
What is it, sire?

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:53.040
There wouldn't happen to be
a woman hiding in these rugs?

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.500
Huh?! Seriously?!

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:05.090
No way, no way! This was gonna be
the surprise of a lifetime!

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:07.260
You're no fun!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:10.890
Leaping out, ready or not,
♪ bum-ba-ba-bum! ♪

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.810
It's Roroa!

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:18.440
Wait, what gave me away?
I was sure you wouldn't be able to notice.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:22.570
Oh, there was a woman once in
my world who did something similar.

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:27.070
Gah! You mean I stole someone
else's act? That's my screw-up.

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:30.200
Incidentally, this woman
was supposedly naked.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.000
What kind of woman was this? Some sicko?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.330
Actually, depending on how
prominent you like your noses,

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:40.380
it's said that she possessed a beauty
that might have changed history.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:44.010
History could have changed
because of the size of her nose?

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:46.760
What are you, taking a shot at my breasts?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:52.020
So, um, may I call you "Roroa"?
The sister of Julius?

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:55.640
Sure. With these fine looks,
having both brains and beauty,

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:00.070
I'm the stone-wearingly stunningly
attractive prettiest girl in Amidonia,

00:22:00.070 --> 00:22:03.360
Roroa! That's who I am!

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:07.530
I am the daughter of the former
Amidonian crown prince, Gaius VIII.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.950
My name is Roroa Amidonia.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:15.210
And what, exactly, would
Princess Roroa be doing here?

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:19.330
I'm here to get married to you.

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:22.130
Oh, you're here to marry me.

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:24.550
Wait, huh?!

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:39.060
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:44.320
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.370
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:59.830
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:05.800
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:13.140
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:17.390
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:23.190
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:28.450
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:32.410
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:46.800
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
